{
  "_doc": "Skill Mods change how a skill behaves. One fit rule (core/skills.js modFits): the skill's visible tags, plus the grants of companion mods that fit the bare skill, must contain ALL of needs, ANY of on (when listed) and NONE of not. Two mods of the same family never share a skill. Each mod has levels 1-3; values are per level. slotsByRank: mod sockets a combat skill has from each skill level in slotLevels on (a skill levels up to the character's level, progression.skillUpgrade). effect.costMult multiplies the skill's MP cost (and a channel's drain) while the mod is active; every combat mod has one (owner, after PoE support gems), mods for movement skills do not. Signature (owner, 2026-10-27): every damage skill with a base cooldown of signatureCooldown s or more is tagged Signature, and a mod that multiplies a cast's hits (more projectiles, repeats, echoes, triggers, a returning shot) lists Signature under not, so the strongest hits are never multiplied.",
